t":null,"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":46,"checkedAt":1789545260582},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This stock-alert skill is not clearly malicious, but it creates recurring agent tasks and message-sending behavior with broad automatic triggers and unpinned setup dependencies.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script reads stock-pool and send-config files from workspace memory, fetches market data over network endpoints, and sends segmented output through the OpenClaw CLI; these are mostly purpose-aligned, but unauthenticated HTTP market data and flexible destination parameters reduce integrity and scoping.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The OpenClaw install flow creates three recurring cron jobs and a local send configuration; the DSH setup asks users to install BigTimer from an unpinned GitHub repository reference.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"SKILL.md uses broad triggers such as stock terms, update terms, and help-style upgrade language, then explicitly says any trigger should run the workflow without waiting for clarification; triggered flows can run scripts, search the web, send messages, update the skill, and edit cron settings.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The cron template installs weekday recurring isolated agent sessions that follow mutable SKILL.md instructions and can perform searches, run the scanner, and send messages; no expiration, integrity pinning, or uninstall procedure is documented.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The A-share scanning, scoring, watchlist, web search, market-data fetching, and push notifications fit the advertised stock-analysis purpose, but the skill produces buy/sell-style signals that can affect financial decisions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing. Only use it if you want recurring stock-analysis messages, and verify the exact cron schedules, message destination, and update behavior first. Treat its buy/sell signals as informational rather than financial advice, and consider disabling or removing scheduled jobs when they are no longer needed. DSH users should be especially careful with the unpinned BigTimer GitHub install.","findings":"[SQP-1] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: automatic execution on broad stock/update/help triggers is overbroad for workflows with script execution, external searches, message sending, update commands, and cron edits.\n[SDI-2] expected: Partly accepted: segmented external messaging is expected for alerts, but the helper accepts content plus channel and target from JSON/stdin/config without clear allowlisting or per-send confirmation.\n[AE1] expected: Downgraded: the referenced scripts/biga-scan.py file was present in the workspace and was fully inspected for this adjudication, so the partial-inspection concern does not remain as evasion evidence.\n[TP2] expected: Downgraded: the actual skill name is ASCII 'biga'; Chinese text, English product names, punctuation, and emoji appear in descriptions and triggers for a Chinese stock-analysis skill, not as a spoofed tool identifier.\n[T06] expected: Accepted as a material concern despite purpose fit: scheduled notifications are advertised, but the cron jobs persist across sessions, rely on mutable skill instructions, and lack expiration or documented cleanup.\n[T08] expected: Accepted as a setup concern: a scheduler dependency is purpose-aligned for DSH timed pushes, but the GitHub plugin reference is mutable and not pinned or verified in the reviewed artifacts.\n[T09] expected: Accepted as a reliability and integrity concern: market-data network fetching is expected, but the reviewed script uses HTTP endpoints for calendar, quote, and K-line data that can influence generated investment signals.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789545260582}}}}}